## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the SmartMess Next.js project.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) via npm
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with all transitive dependencies

**2. Analytics Integration** 
- Modified `app/layout.tsx` to integrate Vercel Web Analytics
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag as per official Next.js App Router documentation

**3. Build Verification**
- Successfully verified the build completes without errors
- Confirmed no linting issues were introduced by the changes
- All tests passed (no test suite was present in the project)

### Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics Quickstart guide for Next.js App Router projects:
- Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Placed the Analytics component at the end of the body tag to avoid blocking page rendering
- Used the recommended `@vercel/analytics/next` import path for Next.js-specific optimizations
- Preserved all existing code structure and formatting

### Files Modified

- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component and import
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree

### Additional Files

The PWA configuration generated service worker files:
- `public/sw.js` - Service worker for PWA functionality
- `public/workbox-f1770938.js` - Workbox library for service worker

These files are generated during the build process and are tracked in git for the PWA functionality.

### Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics → Enable)
2. Visit your deployed site to generate analytics events
3. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab
4. Monitor for XHR requests to `/<unique-path>/view` in browser dev tools to verify tracking is working

The analytics will begin collecting data automatically once the project is deployed to Vercel with analytics enabled in the dashboard.
